    <h1 class="sp-h1" itemprop="headline">Retroreflective vs. Fluorescent: Which Actually Keeps You Visible at Night?</h1>
    <p class="sp-lede">High-visibility yellow looks brilliant in daylight. After dark, it's nearly as invisible as black clothing. Here's the optical science behind each material, and why getting this wrong puts runners, cyclists, and walkers at real risk.</p>
    <p class="sp-research-credit">Based on peer-reviewed research in <em>Human Factors</em> (King et al., 2023) and <em>Accident Analysis &amp; Prevention</em> (Wood et al., 2012).</p>
  </header>

